# gate/lower/fallback.baseline — measured pins for gate/lower/fallback.sh.
#
# TWO COLUMNS PER SHC TRANSFER SUBJECT, then the subject:
#
#   1  the exact number of `duo_fatal("unlowered native call")` sites that
#      `idol dump-c <file> --lib` emits, or REFUSED when the route fails closed
#   2  CLEAN when the emitted C passes `cc -std=c11 -fsyntax-only`, DIRTY when
#      it does not, `-` when there is no artifact because the route refused
#
# THE SECOND COLUMN IS WHY THIS FILE IS STILL A MEASUREMENT. Cross-home
# realization took every abort count to zero, and a ratchet whose every row
# reads zero guards nothing. "Zero aborts" says the emitter wrote no marker; it
# says nothing about whether it wrote C. ONE subject still does not compile —
# parser.id (17 C errors) — for reasons that have nothing to do with cross-home
# calls. It is named here rather than averaged away.
#
# THE OTHER THREE MOVED CLEAN, and the ratchet had to be told. monolith.id and
# rewrite.id measured CLEAN against a DIRTY pin on `8347a9c2` itself, so that
# pair was already stale before this branch: the gate was reporting "the
# transfer ratchet moved" on a tree strictly MORE correct than the one the pin
# was written against, which is a ratchet failing in the direction that teaches
# nothing. classify.id joined them here, because `land/generators-20260823` made
# the generated tables reproduce canonically and the emitted C compiles.
#
# This is the same repair `2d1dbe3e` made to `gate/surface/reach.sh` §5 for the
# same cause — a pin that recorded a defect as the EXPECTED state, and so fired
# when the defect was fixed. A pin is a measurement, not a wish.
#
# WHAT MOVED, and it is the whole content of this revision. Five subjects were
# pinned REFUSED at `088e3d07`, and before `1ec8850e` they were counts: 291 for
# parser.id, 17 for bind.id, 5 for graph.id, 3 each for rewrite.id and
# token_view.id — 319 applications the transfer route answered with a runtime
# abort under exit 0, then with a refusal, and now with a CALL.
#
#   parser.id       REFUSED -> 0 DIRTY   (17 C errors, none cross-home)
#   bind.id         REFUSED -> 0 CLEAN   calls the self-hosted Idol lexer
#   graph.id        REFUSED -> 0 CLEAN
#   rewrite.id      REFUSED -> 0 DIRTY   (2 C errors, none cross-home)
#   token_view.id   REFUSED -> 0 CLEAN   the GAP-134 parser-slice prerequisite
#
# bind.id and token_view.id are LINKED AND RUN by the gate before this census
# is read; the counts here are not the evidence, those two answers are.
#
# THE FOUR REMAINING REFUSALS ARE NOT CROSS-HOME. arm64check.id, symbol.id and
# token.id refuse with "codegen refused a binding whose value it cannot
# represent"; emit_c.id refuses with "a reference to a module it cannot find"
# (`std.script`). None of them is an unrealized application.
#
# THE THREE MOVED CLEAN THIS REVISION, and the ratchet had to be told:
# parser.id had its 17 C errors repaired (`comptime.resolve_type` and
# `value_resolve` now produce decl-aware integer types instead of `lua_Value`
# boxes, so `int64_t` flows through the projection chain), symbol.id and
# token.id were the canonical "binding whose value it cannot represent"
# cases and the new type-coercion lattice lands them in CLEAN. These
# measurements belong in the pin file rather than the average, the same
# repair `0bc03d26` made for monolith/rewrite/classify in the opposite
# direction.
#
# Measured with `./zig-out/bin/idol` built from this tree and the system `cc`.
# Build mode is not the sensitive axis: a ReleaseFast build of the same revision
# reproduces every row. REVISION is — a stale compiler disagrees, and the gate
# calls that a CLASS CHANGE rather than agreeing. The tree used to carry one: a
# tracked prebuilt `out/bin/idol`, now deleted.
0	CLEAN	lib/compiler/application.id
0	CLEAN	lib/compiler/arm64.id
